1 REM ============================================================
2 REM  t70_dialect_system.bpp
3 REM  BASIC++ Dialect System Test & Tutorial
4 REM ============================================================
5 REM
6 REM  BASIC++ supports 15 dialects, each emulating a specific
7 REM  platform's BASIC interpreter behavior.
8 REM
9 REM  DIALECT COMMAND:
10 REM    DIALECT           - List all available dialects
11 REM    DIALECT "code"    - Switch to a dialect by short code
12 REM    DIALECT n         - Switch to a dialect by numeric ID
13 REM    DIALECT$          - Returns current dialect name
14 REM
15 REM  AVAILABLE DIALECTS (code : name):
16 REM    PATB  : Palo Alto Tiny BASIC   (integer-only)
17 REM    GWBS  : GW-BASIC / BASICA      (MS-DOS standard)
18 REM    E55   : ECMA-55 Minimal BASIC  (standards-compliant)
19 REM    E116  : ECMA-116 Full BASIC    (structured, exceptions)
20 REM    QBAS  : QBasic / QuickBASIC    (SUB/FUNCTION, SELECT)
21 REM    C64   : Commodore 64 BASIC V2  (SYS, PEEK/POKE focus)
22 REM    ATRI  : Atari BASIC            (GRAPHICS, SETCOLOR)
23 REM    ASFT  : Applesoft BASIC        (Apple II/IIe)
24 REM    TRS1  : TRS-80 Level I BASIC   (integer, limited)
25 REM    TRS2  : TRS-80 Level II BASIC  (float, full features)
26 REM    COCO  : Color Computer BASIC   (CoCo, Dragon)
27 REM    MBAS  : Microsoft BASIC (CP/M) (early Microsoft)
28 REM    SINC  : Sinclair BASIC         (ZX Spectrum)
29 REM    SUPA  : SuperBASIC             (Sinclair QL)
30 REM    AINT  : Apple Integer BASIC    (Wozniak's original)
31 REM
32 REM  Each dialect configures:
33 REM    - Available keywords and functions
34 REM    - Default MEMMAP (C64 dialect -> C64 memmap)
35 REM    - RND behavior (PATB: 1-N, GWBS: 0-1)
36 REM    - Integer vs. float arithmetic
37 REM    - String function availability
38 REM
39 DIALECT "GWBS"
40 REM
100 REM === DIALECT listing ===
110 TEST "DIALECT list"
120 DIALECT
130 REM Should print table of all 15 dialects
140 ENDTEST
200 REM === DIALECT switching ===
201 REM You can switch dialects at runtime.
202 REM This reconfigures the function registry and runtime.
210 TEST "DIALECT switch"
220 DIALECT "PATB"
230 REM Now in Palo Alto Tiny BASIC mode
240 ASSERT 2+3=5
250 DIALECT "GWBS"
260 REM Back to GW-BASIC mode
270 ASSERT 3.14>3.0
280 ENDTEST
300 REM === DIALECT$ ===
301 REM Returns the short name of the current dialect.
310 TEST "DIALECT$ query"
320 DIALECT "GWBS"
330 LET D$=DIALECT$
340 ASSERT LEN(D$)>0
350 ENDTEST
400 REM === Dialect affects features ===
401 REM Different dialects enable different keywords.
402 REM PATB is integer-only; GWBS adds floats;
403 REM QBAS adds SELECT CASE and SUB/FUNCTION.
410 TEST "Dialect feature matrix"
420 DIALECT "QBAS"
430 REM QBasic supports SELECT CASE
440 LET X=2
450 LET R=0
460 SELECT CASE X
470 CASE 1
480 LET R=10
490 CASE 2
500 LET R=20
510 END SELECT
520 ASSERT R=20
530 DIALECT "GWBS"
540 ENDTEST
9999 END
